      "content": "Consider an `Orders` table with `OrderID`, `CustomerID`, `City`, and `ZipCode`. Here, `City` and `ZipCode` transitively depend on `OrderID` through `CustomerID`, assuming one customer ID maps to only one city/zip. To fix this, you decompose it: keep `Orders` with `OrderID`, `CustomerID`, and remove the city/zip. Create a new `Customers` table containing `CustomerID`, `City`, and `ZipCode`. This isolates the dependency on the customer entity.",
